I guess.
我猜。

00:19:47.519 --> 00:19:52.240
But I said, thank you, it was really expensive.
但我说，谢谢你，它真的很贵。

00:19:52.240 --> 00:19:55.200
And you guys started laughing and I was like, that's funny.
你们开始大笑，我想，这很有趣。

00:19:55.200 --> 00:19:56.440
It was like a nibble.
就像是一口小口。

00:19:56.440 --> 00:19:57.599
It was like a nibble.
就像是一口小口。

00:19:57.599 --> 00:20:00.440
Like I was like, oh my god, they're picking up what I'm putting down.
就像我当时想的那样，天哪，他们正在捡起我放下的东西。

00:20:00.440 --> 00:20:04.519
So much of the time you walk into an audition room and they're like, can you stop making jokes?
很多时候，当你走进试镜室时，他们会问，你能别再开玩笑了吗？

00:20:04.519 --> 00:20:05.880
We're trying to make comedy stuff joking.
我们正在努力让喜剧变成笑话。

00:20:05.880 --> 00:20:07.599
Yeah, exactly.
是的，完全正确。

00:20:07.599 --> 00:20:11.480
But you guys laughed and I was like, oh, like they're here, they're with me.
但你们笑了，我就想，哦，就像他们在这里，他们和我在一起。

00:20:11.480 --> 00:20:13.119
Yeah, yeah, and we were.
是的，是的，我们就是。

00:20:13.119 --> 00:20:14.319
Yeah, and you were.
是的，你也是。

00:20:14.319 --> 00:20:15.880
You know, that's a great observation.
你知道，这是一个很好的观察。

00:20:15.880 --> 00:20:23.200
I had that feeling at my audition to like, these are human beings who are in the room with me.
我在试镜时就有这样的感觉，这些都是和我一起在房间里的人。

00:20:23.200 --> 00:20:32.400
Like sometimes there is that glazed thing of like, oh, I can't do anything to puncture through whatever is the between me and this table.
就像有时会有那种光滑的东西，哦，我无法做任何事情来刺穿我和这张桌子之间的任何东西。

00:20:32.400 --> 00:20:40.000
You know, like, but it's such a relief when you get in front of human beings who see you.
你知道，但是当你站在看到你的人们面前时，你会感到很轻松。

00:20:40.000 --> 00:20:45.119
It's like those are the jobs you get generally or those are the jobs you get close on are like, yeah.
就像这些是你通常得到的工作，或者那些是你接近的工作，是的。

00:20:45.119 --> 00:20:45.634
close it.
关闭它。

00:20:45.634 --> 00:21:03.282
Yeah, but it but it was interesting because like I remember during this time and going back to like your your first initial question, I was deeply in the world of desperately trying to get a job when I booked how I met your mother and I had like and it went on I mean I shot 13 pilots in a row um as the lead.
是的，但这很有趣，因为就像我记得在这段时间里，回到你的第一个最初的问题，当我记录我如何遇见你母亲时，我深深地陷入了拼命寻找工作的世界，我喜欢这样，然后我的意思是我作为主角连续射击了 13 名飞行员。

00:21:03.282 --> 00:21:08.079
I mean it just didn't say it was just every pilot season I was testing twice a week.
我的意思是它只是没有说这只是每个试点赛季我每周测试两次。

00:21:08.079 --> 00:21:13.733
I was I was just right in there and never really it was able to cool on my way and do a secure job.
我当时就在那里，但它从来没有真正能够在我的路上冷却下来并安全地工作。

00:21:13.733 --> 00:21:18.988
And so so much of what I was doing when I was on that set was like, oh my gosh, they did it.
当我在片场时，我所做的很多事情就像是，天哪，他们做到了。

00:21:18.988 --> 00:21:25.156
And I remember like cornering you Josh and being like, did you test how many other test offers did you have?
我记得乔希把你逼到墙角，然后问你有没有测试过你还有多少其他测试机会？

00:21:25.156 --> 00:21:26.184
And how did it go?
进展如何？

00:21:26.184 --> 00:21:27.212
And is this scary?
这可怕吗？

00:21:27.212 --> 00:21:28.183
And are you okay?
你还好吗？

00:21:28.183 --> 00:21:32.409
And I remember it was so much about like, are we, are we going to be okay?
我记得当时很多人都在想，我们，我们会好吗？

00:21:32.409 --> 00:21:37.892
Because you were also like, I don't know, like I don't think many people are watching this show.
因为你也说，我不知道，我认为没有多少人在看这个节目。

00:21:37.892 --> 00:21:40.520
It kind It kind of feels like a little secret.
有点像一个小秘密的感觉。

00:21:40.519 --> 00:21:43.559
Not many of them would have erred by the time you were there, right?
当你在那里的时候，他们中没有多少人会犯错误，对吗？

00:21:43.559 --> 00:21:45.119
We were like, still this new show.
我们就像，仍然是这个新节目。

00:21:45.119 --> 00:21:46.759
Who knew what was going to happen?
谁知道会发生什么？

00:21:46.759 --> 00:21:47.279
Yeah.
是的。

00:21:47.279 --> 00:21:50.839
Well, I was just going to say, I was on set the day that you guys got your back nine.
好吧，我只是想说，你们拿到后九洞的那天我就在片场。

00:21:50.839 --> 00:21:51.599
Oh, wow.
哦，哇。

00:21:51.599 --> 00:21:52.599
I didn't remember that.
我不记得了。

00:21:52.599 --> 00:21:53.119
Yeah.
是的。

00:21:53.119 --> 00:21:53.720
Yeah, that's cool.
是的，那很酷。

00:21:53.720 --> 00:22:00.039
I think you and Carter may have known previously, but the cast didn't know.
我想你和卡特之前可能已经知道了，但演员们不知道。

00:22:00.039 --> 00:22:02.880
And I was there when you came in and made the announcement.
当你进来宣布这一消息时我就在场。

00:22:02.880 --> 00:22:05.160
And it was like such a big deal, you know?
这就像一件大事，你知道吗？

00:22:05.160 --> 00:22:05.519
Yeah.
是的。

00:22:05.519 --> 00:22:11.480
Yeah, oh, that's so weird that you were part of that because you were such a huge part of those back nine episodes, like that was right.
是的，哦，这太奇怪了，你是其中的一部分，因为你是后九集的重要组成部分，就像那是对的。

00:22:11.480 --> 00:22:13.640
I mean, that was, your entry point was right then.
我的意思是，那时你的切入点就是对的。

00:22:13.640 --> 00:22:15.319
It's like, that's so cool.
就好像，这太酷了。

00:22:15.319 --> 00:22:16.519
I'm so glad you're part of that.
我很高兴你参与其中。

00:22:16.519 --> 00:22:30.759
It's also funny to think, Ashley, that you were turning to me as if I was some sort of resident expert on being on a show that lasted, like, it was my first, I had had everything that could have happened to me on a TV show, except it being a long running hit.
想想也很有趣，阿什利，你转向我，就好像我是某种持续演出的常驻专家，就像，这是我的第一次，我在电视节目中经历过一切可能发生在我身上的事情，除了它是一个长期热播的节目。

00:22:30.759 --> 00:22:32.880
Like I got replaced on my first one.
就像我的第一个被替换一样。

00:22:32.880 --> 00:22:34.079
The second one was canceled.
第二个被取消了。

00:22:34.079 --> 00:22:39.680
We shot six, aired three, the third one didn't get picked up, and then I did how I met your mother, right?
我们拍了六部，播出了三部，第三部没拍到，然后我就按照我遇见你妈妈的方式做了，对吧？

00:22:39.680 --> 00:22:44.319
So I was new to the game of, oh, the network wants to keep us on the air.
所以我对这个游戏还是个新手，哦，网络想让我们继续直播。

00:22:44.319 --> 00:22:52.319
Like, that wasn't something I had had any experience with, but I was a part of this thing that just kept working, you know?
就像，这不是我有任何经验的事情，但我是这件事的一部分，一直在工作，你知道吗？

00:22:53.039 --> 00:22:57.559
Well, maybe that was why it was so interesting to me, because you and I were in the same place.
好吧，也许这就是为什么它对我来说如此有趣，因为你和我在同一个地方。

00:22:57.559 --> 00:23:09.400
I had done a couple of shows, a little bit, like the longer you've been at it, Like William Goldman, the screenwriter of, you know, Princess Bride and all these other great things, but he said, no one knows anything.
我做过几部剧，一点点，就像你参与的时间越长，就像威廉·戈德曼（William Goldman）一样，你知道，《公主新娘》和所有其他伟大作品的编剧，但他说，没有人知道任何事情。

00:23:09.400 --> 00:23:17.039
Like famously, he said about Hollywood, like no one knows anything, no one knows why something works, why something doesn't work, something can have all the elements and not work.
正如他在谈到好莱坞时所说的那样，就像没有人知道任何事情一样，没有人知道为什么某些东西有效，为什么某些东西不起作用，某些东西可以拥有所有元素但不起作用。

00:23:17.039 --> 00:23:21.400
Another thing comes out of nowhere, and it's just beloved and embraced and iconic.
另一件事情不知从何而来，它只是受人喜爱、被拥抱和标志性的。

00:23:21.400 --> 00:23:26.480
And I think that we were both in the midst of, like, how do you make this work?
我认为我们都在思考，你如何让这项工作成功？

00:23:26.480 --> 00:23:28.559
How do you get a thing going?
你如何让事情进行下去？

00:23:28.559 --> 00:23:32.019
And you returning to us, like, Hey, you guys seem to have a thing going.
当你回到我们身边时，就像，嘿，你们似乎有事情发生。

00:23:32.019 --> 00:23:32.859
How'd you do it?
你是怎么做到的？

00:23:32.859 --> 00:23:34.420
And we were like, we have no idea.
我们就像，我们不知道。

00:23:34.420 --> 00:23:35.500
We don't know.
我们不知道。

00:23:35.500 --> 00:23:41.980
I did all those, you know, I did all those pilots with like the best of intentions.
我做了所有这些，你知道，我做所有这些飞行员​​都是出于最好的意图。

00:23:41.980 --> 00:23:43.779
Like I was really trying hard.
就像我真的很努力一样。

00:23:43.779 --> 00:23:44.859
I was doing my best.
我已经尽力了。

00:23:44.859 --> 00:23:46.539
I was showing up, you know?
我出现了，你知道吗？

00:23:46.539 --> 00:23:48.019
And this one just worked.
而这个刚刚奏效了。

00:23:48.019 --> 00:23:58.299
So I have a question for you actually like, one of the interesting things I think about doing a long running show is the writers are figuring out who you are as you go.
所以我有一个问题想问你，我认为制作一部长期演出的有趣的事情之一是编剧们正在弄清楚你是谁。

00:23:58.299 --> 00:24:11.099
And they're also, we've talked a little bit about this, like you have an idea, like for instance, Marshall was not written to be six foot four, but then Jason Siegel gets cast and his height becomes a vein of comedy they can mine.
我们也对此进行了一些讨论，就像你有一个想法一样，例如，马歇尔的身高不是六英尺四英寸，但后来杰森·西格尔被选为演员，他的身高成为他们可以挖掘的喜剧脉络。

00:24:11.099 --> 00:24:14.380
He was written to be seven feet tall, but Jason was a little shorter than that.
他被写为七英尺高，但杰森比这个矮一点。

00:24:14.380 --> 00:24:21.900
Right, but you came on and they had this idea for this character and then you're obviously, you're affecting the writing as they go.
是的，但是你来了，他们对这个角色有了这个想法，然后你显然，你正在影响他们的写作。

00:24:21.900 --> 00:24:37.079
They're tailoring this suit to you, but also you as an actor are opening up that new draft for the next episode and you're like, oh, Victoria, she applied for a baking fellowship and you're like, you're learning new things about who this person is.
他们正在为你量身定制这套衣服，但你作为演员正在为下一集打开新的草稿，你就像，哦，维多利亚，她申请了烘焙奖学金，你就像，你正在学习关于这个人是谁的新知识。

00:24:37.079 --> 00:24:42.359
Was that, do you remember that as like a thing of like kind of discovering it as you go?
那是吗，你还记得那是一种边走边发现的事情吗？

00:24:42.359 --> 00:24:56.119
Well, that's one of my favorite things about TV is, you know, what I always felt like, I always feel like when I come into audition for a TV show, I'm going, all right, if you choose the Ashley Williams path, here's the path that you're gonna get, you know?
嗯，这是我对电视最喜欢的事情之一，你知道，我一直觉得，当我参加电视节目试镜时，我总是觉得，我会，好吧，如果你选择阿什利·威廉姆斯的道路，这就是你会走的路，你知道吗？

00:24:56.119 --> 00:24:59.940
like here's the little pockets that you can go into.
就像这是你可以放进去的小口袋。

