If we had had two more, we would have had two more fun episodes with you that rather than like the arc we'd sort of booked you for and written and planned out.
如果我们再有两集，我们就会和你一起看两集更有趣的剧集，而不是像我们为你预订、编写和计划的弧线那样。

00:35:02.960 --> 00:35:05.119
But did you like, was that hard?
但你喜欢吗，这很难吗？

00:35:05.119 --> 00:35:08.440
Was that hard to kind of parachute in and try to feel like part of the team?
跳伞并尝试融入团队是不是很困难？

00:35:08.440 --> 00:35:13.800
Cause it seemed from the outside, like you were immediately in and felt like part of the team.
因为从外面看，你就像是立即融入团队并感觉自己是团队的一部分。

00:35:13.800 --> 00:35:16.440
That is first of all, such a nice compliment.
首先，这是一个很好的赞美。

00:35:20.079 --> 00:35:31.320
It was entirely because, and I say this as a person now, And not this was not true at the time, but now I've been a guest star like 200 times.
这完全是因为，我现在作为一个人这么说，当时并不是这样，但现在我已经客串了大约 200 次。

00:35:31.320 --> 00:35:39.760
Like I've literally done 200 guest art episodes where I come in for just a couple, little recurings, little, you know, a one off of whatever.
就像我实际上已经完成了 200 集客座艺术剧集一样，其中我只参加了几集，一点点重复，一点点，你知道，无论什么都是一次性的。

00:35:39.760 --> 00:35:42.920
Like that's been my career, you know?
这就是我的职业生涯，你知道吗？

00:35:42.920 --> 00:35:57.800
So I am now, so I find it so second nature to show up on a set and immediately start learning people's names and listen very intently to like the culture and the subtext and kind of, you smell it before you see it.
现在我就是这样，所以我发现出现在片场并立即开始学习人们的名字并非常专心地聆听喜欢文化和潜台词以及某种程度的第二天性，你在看到它之前就闻到了它。

00:35:57.800 --> 00:36:01.159
You know what I mean, like it's really like figuring it.
你知道我的意思，就像它真的就像在计算它一样。

00:36:01.159 --> 00:36:04.800
It's really every, yeah, every set is completely different.
确实，每一组都是完全不同的。

00:36:04.800 --> 00:36:15.199
And learning each set's culture is something that has really, I mean, it's taken a long time for me to really get good at.
我的意思是，学习每个系列的文化确实需要很长时间才能真正擅长。

00:36:15.199 --> 00:36:29.159
And now interestingly enough, I'm now an episodic director and it's what I think is one of my assets as an episodic director is I can come on and immediately go, ooh, okay, so he said that guy's in charge.
有趣的是，我现在是一名剧集导演，我认为作为一名剧集导演，我的资产之一就是我可以上场并立即离开，哦，好吧，所以他说那个人负责。

00:36:29.159 --> 00:36:34.519
We're scared of her, you know, and just immediately start picking up on all the cues.
你知道，我们很害怕她，所以我们立即开始捕捉所有的线索。

00:36:34.519 --> 00:36:54.159
But I have to say, your set was really different than that because immediately, I mean, I remember my first day, so after Pam took us all the breakfast, then Ali took me through and gave me a tour of the entire stage.
但我不得不说，你的布景真的很不一样，因为我立刻就记得我的第一天，所以在帕姆带我们吃完早餐后，阿里带我参观了整个舞台。

00:36:54.159 --> 00:37:04.800
She was like, here's where all your dressing rooms, here's the dressing rooms, here's her makeup, here are all the different sets, and she showed me where the bathrooms were, where the turkey bacon was.
她说，这是所有更衣室的地方，这是更衣室，这是她的化妆品，这是所有不同的布景，她向我展示了浴室在哪里，火鸡培根在哪里。

00:37:04.800 --> 00:37:15.239
It was the very, she immediately made me feel so at home, and it was a priority of the whole cast to do that, and that is not normally the case.
她立即​​让我感到宾至如归，这是整个演员的首要任务，但通常情况并非如此。

00:37:15.239 --> 00:37:21.400
Normally, I guess, it feels like a threat to the cast, And I was not made to feel like that at all.
通常情况下，我想，这感觉像是对演员的威胁，而我根本没有被要求有这样的感觉。

00:37:21.400 --> 00:37:22.519
It's so true what you're saying.
你说的太对了

00:37:22.519 --> 00:37:30.760
I haven't guest-starred that much, but when I have, it's incredibly, it's like, it's beyond first day of school vibes.
我客串过的次数不多，但当我客串过的时候，这真是令人难以置信，就像，这超出了开学第一天的氛围。

00:37:30.760 --> 00:37:34.400
Like it is, you are, because not, it's not everyone's first day of school.
就像它是，你是，因为不是，这不是每个人上学的第一天。

00:37:34.400 --> 00:37:36.360
It's just your first day of school.
这只是你上学的第一天。

00:37:36.360 --> 00:37:42.480
So you're entering this ecosystem that really does have its own bylaws and its own language.
所以你正在进入这个生态系统，它确实有自己的章程和自己的语言。

00:37:42.480 --> 00:37:43.920
And it's like, you're a tourist.
就像，你是一名游客。

00:37:43.920 --> 00:37:46.679
So I commend you for doing that 200 times.
所以我赞扬你这样做了 200 次。

00:37:46.679 --> 00:37:49.440
Like, it's really a big thing.
比如说，这确实是一件大事。

00:37:49.440 --> 00:37:51.039
I don't love doing it, to be honest.
老实说，我不喜欢这样做。

00:37:51.039 --> 00:37:57.239
I like having the thing where it's like, you come to my home, I don't like to come to yours, you know.
我喜欢这样的事情，你来我家，我不喜欢来你家，你知道。

00:37:57.239 --> 00:37:58.079
I don't know.
我不知道。

00:37:58.079 --> 00:38:00.159
I think it's fun, you know.
我觉得这很有趣，你知道。

00:38:00.159 --> 00:38:04.719
But I also, you know, I really love, like I really love what we do.
但我也，你知道，我真的很喜欢，就像我真的很喜欢我们所做的那样。

00:38:04.719 --> 00:38:07.280
I think it is the most fun.
我认为这是最好玩的。

00:38:07.280 --> 00:38:16.400
So coming in and cracking how each set tells their story is just some of the most fun in the world, because it, but it all is the same.
因此，进入并破解每个场景如何讲述他们的故事只是世界上最有趣的事情之一，因为它，但一切都是一样的。

00:38:16.400 --> 00:38:26.619
And you know, I will, I will say this actually, this is just occurring to me, but this feels very true to me is that, you know, I was working, especially in the first season, I was, I was nervous.
你知道，我会，我实际上会这么说，这只是发生在我身上，但这对我来说非常真实，你知道，我在工作，特别是在第一季，我很紧张。

00:38:26.619 --> 00:38:30.940
I was, you know, I'm a good student, like I wanted to do well, right?
我是，你知道，我是一个好学生，就像我想做得很好，对吧？

00:38:30.940 --> 00:38:40.460
But it's also like the role and acting generally requires a certain amount of looseness and risk and fit, you know, acceptance of failure and like it's all going to be.
但这也就像角色和表演通常需要一定程度的放松、风险和配合，你知道，接受失败，就像一切都会这样。

00:38:40.460 --> 00:38:56.900
And you, what I think you bring to a set, and this is why I think you've been so employable, is that I got the feeling like whenever you were on set, there's a little bit of a feeling underneath everything you do, which is like, can you believe we're getting away with this and that they're paying us to do this?
而你，我认为你给片场带来的，这就是为什么我认为你如此受雇的原因，是我有一种感觉，就像每当你在片场时，你所做的一切背后都有一种感觉，就像是，你能相信我们能逃脱惩罚吗？他们付钱给我们来做这件事？

00:38:56.900 --> 00:39:03.380
Like there's a feeling of like, like this is insane that this is our career.
就像有一种感觉，就像这是我们的职业，这太疯狂了。

00:39:03.380 --> 00:39:07.340
Like this thing we just like doing as kids, we now get to do as adults.
就像我们小时候喜欢做的事情一样，现在我们成年人也可以做。

00:39:07.340 --> 00:39:09.300
And that's the best it should feel that way.
这就是最好的感觉。

00:39:09.300 --> 00:39:19.980
And it reminded me that like, as this guy I know who passed away, but this guy, Evio Tar-Frankle, who his kind of catchphrase was it's supposed to be fun.
这让我想起，就像我认识的这个人去世了一样，但是这个人，埃维奥·塔尔-弗兰克尔，他的口头禅是这应该很有趣。

00:39:19.980 --> 00:39:22.099
Remember it's supposed to be fun.
请记住，这应该很有趣。

00:39:22.099 --> 00:39:26.579
And I feel like whenever you were on set, it was a reminder to me like it's supposed to be fun.
我觉得无论何时你在片场，都会提醒我这应该很有趣。

00:39:26.579 --> 00:39:27.579
Yeah.
是的。

00:39:27.579 --> 00:39:28.420
Yeah.
是的。

00:39:28.420 --> 00:39:30.019
Oh, that's so cool.
哦，那太酷了。

00:39:30.019 --> 00:39:31.019
I love that.
我喜欢那个。

00:39:31.019 --> 00:39:40.900
Well, I remember when I first, one of my first days with Pam, I was like, tell me, because again, like coming from the intense multi-cam world, I was like, tell me about these show runners.
嗯，我记得当我第一次，和帕姆在一起的第一天，我想，告诉我，因为，就像来自激烈的多镜头世界一样，我想，告诉我关于这些节目主持人的事情。

00:39:40.900 --> 00:39:42.099
Like, are they safe?
比如，他们安全吗？

00:39:42.099 --> 00:39:42.980
Like, are they nice?
比如，他们好吗？

00:39:42.980 --> 00:39:44.539
What's going on with them?
他们怎么了？

00:39:44.539 --> 00:39:46.139
They were talking about my shirt and casting.
他们正在谈论我的衬衫和选角。

00:39:46.139 --> 00:39:47.500
Do I have something to be worried about?
我有什么需要担心的吗？

00:39:47.500 --> 00:39:50.460
Yeah, well, I was, I was just like, what do I have to be aware of?
是的，好吧，我是，我只是想，我必须注意什么？

00:39:50.460 --> 00:39:54.380
And Pam said, they just can't believe there's craft service.
帕姆说，他们简直不敢相信还有工艺品服务。

00:39:54.380 --> 00:39:59.099
And that was such a great line about you guys.
这对你们来说真是太好了。

00:39:59.099 --> 00:40:02.340
They really set the tone, I think, for everybody.
我认为他们确实为每个人定下了基调。

00:40:02.340 --> 00:40:10.219
But yeah, I agree, Josh, like getting any acting job, I feel like I'm like, I cannot believe we put this off.
但是，是的，我同意，乔什，就像得到任何表演工作一样，我觉得我不敢相信我们推迟了这件事。

00:40:10.219 --> 00:40:15.340
Like how long before they come in and say, get the heck out of here, you crazy person.
就像过了多久他们就会进来并说，滚出去，你这个疯子。

00:40:15.340 --> 00:40:16.820
Who do you think you are?
你以为你是谁？

00:40:16.820 --> 00:40:20.699
But every day we get away with another day on set.
但每天我们都会在片场多度过一天。

00:40:20.699 --> 00:40:26.860
I'm like, I can't believe they're not coming in and yelling at us and saying that we're ahead of our skis.
我想，我不敢相信他们没有进来对我们大喊大叫，说我们领先于我们的滑雪板。

00:40:26.860 --> 00:40:33.219
God, that is the best description of what it means to stay curious and creative.
天啊，这就是对保持好奇心和创造力的最好描述。

00:40:33.219 --> 00:40:34.099
That is what it is.
就是这样。

00:40:34.099 --> 00:40:35.460
How do we get to do this?
我们怎样才能做到这一点？

00:40:35.460 --> 00:40:37.179
How are we this lucky?
我们怎么这么幸运？

00:40:37.179 --> 00:40:39.659
And at its best, that's what art feels like.
在最好的情况下，这就是艺术的感觉。

00:40:39.659 --> 00:40:51.260
And you really do kind of exude that Like even like when you come and you sing with us, actually comes and she sings for these, the fundraiser that's really important to my, to my world and my family, it's sort of for my son.
你确实散发出一种感觉，甚至就像当你来和我们一起唱歌时，她真的来了，她为这些筹款活动唱歌，这对我、我的世界和我的家庭来说非常重要，这有点像是为了我的儿子。

00:40:51.260 --> 00:40:52.739
And she comes and sings and performs.
她来唱歌、表演。

00:40:52.739 --> 00:40:55.260
And it just feels that way, just you getting up and sing a song with us.
就是这样的感觉，只要你站起来和我们一起唱一首歌。

00:40:55.260 --> 00:40:56.099
It feels that way.
感觉就是这样。

00:40:56.099 --> 00:40:57.860
Like it's, I love that.
就像它一样，我喜欢这样。

00:40:57.860 --> 00:40:58.699
I love that.
我喜欢那个。

00:40:58.699 --> 00:41:00.300
That's so precious.
那真是太珍贵了。

00:41:00.300 --> 00:41:04.139
When you first said, you know, Bowery Ballroom, what was it years ago?
当你第一次说，你知道，鲍厄里宴会厅，几年前是什么？

00:41:04.139 --> 00:41:08.179
I was like, I am not a singer, Craig.
我当时想，我不是歌手，克雷格。

00:41:08.179 --> 00:41:09.019
Like I don't.
就像我不一样。

00:41:09.019 --> 00:41:10.019
Or a tough dancer.
或者是一个坚强的舞者。

00:41:10.019 --> 00:41:11.219
Or much of a kisser.
或者说是一个接吻者。

00:41:11.219 --> 00:41:28.030
But I'm not going to turn down the opportunity as a quintessentially non-singer.
但作为一个典型的非歌手，我不会拒绝这个机会。

00:41:28.030 --> 00:41:29.030
People say, Oh, do you sing?
人们说，哦，你唱歌吗？

00:41:29.030 --> 00:41:39.869
And I say, I sing enthusiastically, but not well, and so I'm getting to get up on stage at the Bellery Ballroom and being as untalented as a singer as I am.
我说，我唱歌很热情，但唱得不好，所以我要登上贝勒里舞厅的舞台，像我一样没有歌手的天赋。

00:41:39.869 --> 00:41:41.670
It's just too funny to me.
这对我来说太有趣了。

00:41:41.670 --> 00:41:43.230
It's too funny.
太搞笑了。

00:41:43.230 --> 00:41:44.789
You were a living yes and.
你是一个活生生的人。

00:41:44.789 --> 00:41:46.429
You were a living breathing yes and.
你是一个活生生的呼吸者，是的，而且。

00:41:46.429 --> 00:41:47.989
Aw, thanks.
噢，谢谢。

00:41:47.989 --> 00:41:51.989
Hey everyone, we had so much great Ashley Williams that we've actually made this one a two-parter.
大家好，我们有很多很棒的阿什利·威廉姆斯，所以我们实际上把这部剧做成了两部剧。

00:41:51.989 --> 00:41:57.550
So come on back in about three days to hear part two of how we met Ashley Williams.
所以大约三天后回来听听我们如何认识阿什利·威廉姆斯的第二部分。

